      "content": "## Roman Numeral Rules\n\n### The Seven Roman Numeral Letters\n- **I** = 1\n- **V** = 5\n- **X** = 10\n- **L** = 50\n- **C** = 100\n- **D** = 500\n- **M** = 1000\n\n### Rules for Combining\n1. **Smaller numbers before larger numbers are subtracted** (e.g., IV = 4, IX = 9)\n2. **Smaller numbers after larger numbers are added** (e.g., VI = 6, XI = 11)\n3. **Roman numerals have no zero**\n4. **Large numbers** are indicated with a horizontal line above them, multiplying the value by 1000"
